{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Calah</b> — to do violence he comes." "And the word <b>megamat</b> is foreign. And it is possible that it is like <i>yigma eretz</i> ['the land is gathered'] — and behold it is like <i>neged</i> and <i>negiah</i> ['facing' and 'in front of']." "And the word <b>qedimah</b> is difficult, for he comes from the direction of the east. Therefore Japheth needed to add a kaph: <i>ke-qedimah</i> ['like the east wind'], like <i>ruach qadim</i>, which is strong. And there is no argument from the he, for behold <i>yashuvu resha'im she'olah</i> [the wicked will return to Sheol] and many others."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:50.596061969Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}